error[type]: function 'w' is defined again with another type, and 'gw' uses it
 --> <repl:13>:1:4
   |
 1 | fn w(x: a) -> String where a: Tb + Ta { "{Tb.tb(x)}{Ta.ta(x)}" }
   |    ^ function 'w' is defined again with another type, and 'gw' uses it
  = note: it was Fn(a) -> String where a: Ta + Tb, and is Fn(a) -> String where a: Tb + Ta here
  = note: a function defined again replaces the old one for every caller, so it keeps its type
  = help: write its bounds in the old order (a: Ta + Tb)
